{
  // harness-jobs — DB-driven job/stage/budget coordination for the fleet.
  // Its OWN worker, like harness-locks and harness-watchdog: a bad deploy here
  // must never be able to take down the console or the Telegram relay.
  // Spec: docs/DB-COORDINATION-SPEC.md. Deploy notes: worker/jobs/README.md.
  "name": "harness-jobs",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-01",
  // @sentry/cloudflare imports node:async_hooks and other node: modules
  // (BH-5618). Without this flag wrangler warns and the bundle is wrong.
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  // BH-4987: src/lib/schema-sql.workerd.js imports the composed schema.sql as
  // text, and CREATED_TABLES (src/lib/core.js) derives from it.
  "rules": [{ "type": "Text", "globs": ["**/*.sql"], "fallthrough": true }],
  // BH-4607: src/index.js imports ROUTES from "#routes", which is the
  // git-ignored src/routes.gen.js under wrangler. This renders it from
  // test/route-table.d/ before every bundle; a refused fragment fails the deploy.
  // BH-8395: src/lib/core.js imports ADDED_COLUMNS/ADDED_INDEXES from
  // "#core-registries", the git-ignored src/lib/core-registries.gen.js, rendered from src/lib/core.d/.
  "build": { "command": "node scripts/routes-build.mjs && node scripts/core-registries-build.mjs" },
  "account_id": "00000000000000000000000000000000",
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "d1_databases": [
    { "binding": "DB", "database_name": "harness-jobs", "database_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000" }
    // BH-6774: the archive store (src/lib/archive.js). Commented out until the
    // database exists: a binding with no real database_id fails every deploy,
    // and harness-sync deploys this worker on every sync. With it absent the
    // worker moves nothing to the archive and deletes nothing an archive rule
    // owns. Operator steps (once): `npx wrangler d1 create harness-archive`
    // (from worker/jobs), paste its database_id below, uncomment the line
    // (and the comma above it), deploy. The worker creates the archive tables.
    // ,{ "binding": "ARCHIVE", "database_name": "harness-archive", "database_id": "<id from wrangler d1 create harness-archive>" }
  ],
  // BH-5781: seconds an isolate reuses its settings snapshot (0..60, 0 = off).
  // The `settings_cache_ttl_s` settings row overrides it. See src/lib/settings-cache.js.
  "vars": { "SETTINGS_CACHE_TTL_S": "30" }
  // secrets (wrangler secret put, never in this file):
  //   HARNESS_SECRET — the same bearer every box already holds.
  //   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET — the HMAC key for POST /webhooks/github, shared
  //     with the org-level GitHub webhook and with nothing else. Set it with
  //     `wrangler secret put GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (the value is typed, never
  //     committed, never echoed). UNSET IS THE SAFE STATE: the receiver answers
  //     503 and writes no rows, so the fleet keeps ticking on cron alone.
  //     Full ops steps: docs/EVENTS.md.
  //   HARNESS_SENTRY_DSN — the Sentry DSN this worker reports exceptions to
  //     (BH-5618). UNSET = no reporting, and the SDK is never loaded. Kill
  //     switch without a deploy: the pause_flags row lane-off-sentry-report
  //     with active=1, or `wrangler secret delete HARNESS_SENTRY_DSN`.
  //     Optional plain var HARNESS_SENTRY_MAX_PER_FP_HOUR (default 6).
  //     Optional plain vars HARNESS_D1_GIVEUP_REPORT_AFTER (default 3) and
  //     HARNESS_D1_GIVEUP_WINDOW_S (default 900): a verdict route's D1
  //     overload give-up reports only on every Nth give-up of a streak
  //     (lib/d1-giveup.js, BH-7541).
  //   ENVELOPE_HUB_TOKEN — the hub-only token for GET /api/secrets/envelope/<id>
  //     (BH-7964). The hub holds the same value in /etc/harness/env/global.env.
  //     UNSET IS THE SAFE STATE: the read answers 503. See
  //     docs/notes/2026-10-22-BH-7964-secret-envelopes.md.
}
